(ARG-26 — with `Parse flags.` omitted, parsing is inserted automatically
 immediately after the LAST flag schema declaration
 (LANGUAGE.md:4489). Reading a flag after the last schema works with no
 parse statement anywhere in the file.
 Also covers: ARG-27 (a schema is valid as long as it precedes parsing)
 and ARG-28 (ordinary code before and between schema declarations is
 allowed — both Prints below sit inside the schema block and run).
 The "immediately after the LAST one" half of the claim is what
 ARG-31.vox proves from the other side: a flag read placed BETWEEN two
 schema declarations is rejected as a use before the parse point.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox ARG-26.vox -o p && ./p -v -o mine
 Args: -v -o mine
 expected output:
   code before the schema
   code between the schemas
   verbose is 1
   output is mine
)
Print "code before the schema".
a flag called verbose is "-v" or "--verbose", it is a boolean.
Print "code between the schemas".
a flag called output is "-o" or "--output", it is a text with default "auto".
Print "verbose is {verbose}".
Print "output is {output}".
